      "Note attachment behaviors between parent and child(ren), recognizing cultural background. Beha viors such as ey eto-eye contact, use of en face position, and talking to the infant in a high-pitched voice are indicative of attachment behaviors in American culture but may not be practiced in another culture. Nursing Priority No. 2. To enhance behavioral organization of the infant/child:",
