      "Atypical presentations in older adults [e.g., changes in mental status, urinary incontinence, unexplained falls, elevated body temperature] Borborygmi; hypoactive or hyperactive bowel sounds Hard, formed stool; presence of soft pastelike stool in rectum; liquid stool; straining with defecation Bright red blood with stool; liquid stool Percussed abdominal dullness; palpable abdominal or rectal mass Severe fl atus Associated Condition: Electrolyte imbalance; iron salts Hemorrhoids; Hirschprung’s disease; postsurgical bowel obstruction; prostate enlargement; tumor Neurological impairment; pregnancy Rectal abscess; rectal anal fi ssure or stricture; rectal ulcer Rectal prolapse; rectocele"
