      "Assess an older client’s “hydration habits” to determine the best appr oach if the client has potential for dehydration. Note: A recent study identifi ed four categories of nursing home residents: (1) can drink (the client is functionally capable of consuming fl uids, but does not for any number of reasons); (2) cannot drink (frailty or dysphagia makes this client incapable of consuming fl uids safely); (3) will not drink (client may fear incontinence or may have never in life consumed many fl uids); and (4) end of life.",
