      "Encourage the client/signifi cant other (SO) to record times at which incontinence occurs to note r elationship to meals, activity, medications, or client’s behavior.",
      "Auscultate abdomen f or pr esence, location, and characteristics of bowel sounds. Nursing Priority No. 3. To promote control/management of incontinence:",
      "Assist in the treatment of causative/contributing factors. Although incontinence is a symptom and not a disease, appr opriate treatment can often correct the problem or at least improve the client’s quality of life.",
