      "Note client report of potential for alteration of habitual sleep time (e.g., change of w ork pattern, rotating shifts) or change in normal bedtime (e.g., hospitalization). Helps identify cir cumstances that are known to interrupt sleep patterns and that could disrupt the person’s biological rhythms. Nursing Priority No. 2. To assist client to enhance sleep/rest:",
      "Review client’s usual bedtime rituals, routines, and sleep environment needs. Pr ovides information on client’s management of the situation and identifi es areas that might be modifi ed when the need arises.",
